WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.190
Peking,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.690
Berlin,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.230
Dublin,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.020
Liberia...

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.530
Hey, Souma!

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.200
You're dressed like some drifter. What are you doing?

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.950
When was the last time you came to university?

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.200
You went traveling again, didn't you?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.200
Hey, Long-hair.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.750
Don't call me "Long-hair."

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.040
What are you doing?

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.710
I was deciding where to go next.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.580
Making a decision already?

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.580
You off again?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.960
You haven't changed at all.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.300
It doesn't matter.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.880
I'm researching how far a man's love for maps can take him.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.180
Liar.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.850
Everyone reckons that you're eventually going to quit university.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.230
Kaneda from our seminar group was sulking.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.230
Give him a call sometime, will you?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.100
Sure.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.110
Long-hair!

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.150
Well, I'm heading off to class.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.480
Take it easy with the roaming, okay?

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.780
Or you'll end up as a duckweed.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.570
Even if you tell me that...

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.330
What's up?

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.160
Did you forget something-

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.960
What's a tiny angel doing... on campus?

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.970
Can you tell me where the staff room is?

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:26.850
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.660
Just one word is fine.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.540
Just voice your dreams.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.670
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.750
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.880
Your answers will...

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.890
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.300
Even more...

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.180
Like fireworks...

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:05.390
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:12.400
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.950
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:24.080
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:30.040
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:38.260
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.510
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.020
People often ask me what "manimani" means.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.020
It means something like "to let matter take its own course."

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:55.020
It's not to follow the recent fad of using four hiragana characters in the title.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:55.020
Also, you don't read the kanji as "chuu" or "hiroshi."

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.150
Saku!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.410
Saku, it's dinner time!

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.200
I wonder what's wrong with him...

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.750
He isn't even watching "808 District, Rough Thief Alley: Shooting Star Sonata."

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.870
Why?

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.840
Why did I say that?!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.470
Um, I've got some stuff that other people asked me to help out with.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.550
Can I help them out too?

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.720
In no way is it compulsory to help the Literature Club!

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.100
She even phrased it in such a way that I'd only be lending a hand.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:32.850
Would you...

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.110
like to help out too?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:42.030
There was absolutely no reason for me to pour cold water on the Astronomy Club's activity!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.740
But with her saying that...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.040
What?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.620
Why... Saku-chan?

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.460
When we all...

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.630
It's for the Literature Club.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.550
They asked me to help them with their literature magazine for the cultural festival.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.760
Apparently, it'll be different from previous years because it'll include works that were written after our joint activity...

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:09.890
That's why...

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:12.980
That's...

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.610
If that's the case, then I guess we have no choice!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.440
And the way she said it...

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:26.030
Rather, it's like you were chosen to be the ambassador for the Astronomy Club, Saku-chan!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.620
Actually, a diplomat!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.120
A bridge!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.910
What are you saying?!

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.160
Please stop him!

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.540
You're amazing!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:33.960
What is?!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.420
If that's the case, you should help them.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.040
What is?!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.000
Amazing!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.040
Stop him!

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:37.670
Stop him!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.420
But make sure you help us out when we need the manpower.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:42.010
Stop him! Stop him! Stop him! Stop him! Stop him!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:41.510
Got it?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.590
Yes.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.090
Stop laughing!

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.680
Well, because of this, I have a girl on each arm, plus one extra; I'm so happy.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.260
Now, come along everyone.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.060
Let's start from the beginning.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.060
From the beginning!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.690
Give up!

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.270
But I think... I'll decline after all...

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.070
Kotodzuka-senpai!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.570
I-It's about what you asked me yesterday.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.120
I'll help.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.090
Come in. Come in.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.930
Welcome.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.800
Kotodzuka-senpai told us all about you.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:30.850
What's up?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.270
T-Thank you for inviting me...

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.900
This is amazing.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.570
This is completely different from the Astronomy Club.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.610
From editing to layout, we do everything.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.120
Our Literature Club is quite famous around this area.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.370
During the cultural festival, we not only sell our literature magazine,

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.710
but we also provide other activities such as inviting authors as guest speakers and story-telling.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.790
We've always placed high in the best event competition.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.040
Really?

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.550
So, what should I do?

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.970
Um, you see, we decided to publish two magazines this year.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.340
We'd like you to help us with this one.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.850
First, we need a title.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.980
We want to use the name of a star. Will you suggest one?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.310
What we all saw were the summer constellations,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:20.730
so how about Vega?

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.690
It's spelled V-E-G-A.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.530
V-E-G-A! I like that!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.110
It's pronounced "veɪgə."

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.820
"Veɪgə"? Okay!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.660
It means "falling eagle" in Arabic, but the word is feminine, so it has a soft ring to it.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.950
"Falling eagle," gotcha!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.960
Not bad.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:44.920
Senpai!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.130
Please continue to do your best.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.260
Senpai, I'm having problems with this.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:51.930
Oh, that.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.140
That's when you make it three columns.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.480
Oh, she's so cool.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:03.520
We have an official Literature Club President, but in reality, Kotodzuka-senpai runs everything.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.190
She must be really popular.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.200
Now, now, let's do our best!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.410
Oh, that's right. We'd like people from the Astronomy Club to write their thoughts too.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.080
Could you ask them on our behalf?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.830
Texas.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:23.630
New York!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.840
San Francisco!

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.550
Las Vegas!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.010
Wow! It's huge! It's huge!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.060
So, this will be our fortress for a while.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.600
It's normal inside.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:40.770
Yup, it's normal inside.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.140
It's normal inside!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.230
Nice going, Cultural Festival Committee and Student Council.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.270
Now, now, Makita.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.280
I know how you feel, but let's do our best.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.030
You're the only first year we have right now.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.860
I know that!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:53.780
Good.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.740
Sou-nii, is the dome going over here?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.660
Will it fill the whole class?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:03.960
The ceiling is approximately three meters high, so if we utilize the height of this room,

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.750
it'll be around three to five meters in diameter.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.710
That should fit around ten people.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.380
What about the projector?

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.630
It'll be a pin-hole planetarium.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.050
It works by projecting stars to its surrounding area via small holes.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:22.140
If we make holes in a cooking bowl and place a light underneath the bowl, it should be sufficient.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.480
Although if we want to make it more like the original, it'll be a bit more difficult.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.990
As a side note, this is how much we have to spend.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.400
So little!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.950
Don't worry!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:39.410
We, kids of the Heisei era, have Hyakkin stores!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:39.410
[Note: Hyakkin stores are like 1 dollar stores but every item is 100 yen.]

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.620
If we believe we can get anything, we <i>can</i> get anything!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.210
We can get anything!

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:43.540
That's true.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.670
Let's visit the store and do some research.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.080
Yup!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.960
If you're going shopping, can I go back to the Photography Club?

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.760
Hey! Have you forgotten your promise to us?!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.510
But I'm a member of the Photography Club...

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.510
Why, you!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.220
Both of you, calm down.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.800
You really irritate me!

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.640
I <i>am</i> calm!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.390
Saku-chan's one lucky guy.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.220
Hey!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.140
All right!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.310
In that case, the four of us will go and do some research.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.780
All right, I'll go get my car.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:12.740
Really?

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.790
Practicing photography using photos of gravure models.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.370
Practice is hard indeed.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.120
Next, I need to practice modeling-

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.080
Say, does Ooyagi-kun like mature women?

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.540
Answer me honestly.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.220
W-W-What happened?!

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.300
W-Who are you referring to?!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.720
Did you catch a cold?

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.230
Oh, Sayo-chin, what about this one?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.190
Is it too big? Too small?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.610
Mihoshi, are you okay?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.070
About what?

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.070
"About what?"

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.780
I'm fine, Sayo-chin.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.620
After all, we're both doing the exact same thing.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.830
It's not like he's going to disappear.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.710
Besides, if we don't have fun, he'll be troubled when he comes back.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:15.760
Also, Sou-nii joined us, and this year we're doing something that was unthinkable for us till now.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.680
You're right. Let's do our best.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.350
That reminds me, where are the President and Souma-sensei?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.810
They said they would keep an eye on the car.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.770
Apparently, parking is prohibited there.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.060
We've made progress.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.070
For today, let's call it a day.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:34.480
Want to eat something on our way home?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.240
Erm... I'll pass.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.530
Why?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:39.200
Mos Burger! Mos Burger!

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.910
You know, you get a 100 yen off today.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:42.700
Really?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:42.740
Really?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.680
Oh, they've already gone home...

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.730
Summer vacation feels like it was so long ago...

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.120
Mi-

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.830
I came to get something I forgot.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.420
How are things going your end?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:35.250
Is everything going okay?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.800
Erm... yeah...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:37.500
Bye!

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.460
Um... Hey-!

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.030
Then, what color does Ooyagi-kun like?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.530
Either blue or red.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.490
What's his favorite food?

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.370
Curry.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.120
Ask me anything!

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.330
W-What type of girl does he like?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.040
[Note: This is a pun on Yasu Megumi a Japanese gravure model.]

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.380
Yadzu Megumi.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.960
I'm positive.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.340
The gleam in his eyes when he looks at a gravure magazine with her on the front cover-

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.800
That kind of information is useless!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.220
What?!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:27.970
Mi...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.350
Mii-chan?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.060
W-Why?

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.570
H-Huh?

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.150
Um... Er...

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.200
No!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:50.120
What is this?!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.250
Ooyagi-kun and the short sophomore?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.410
Discord between blind passion?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.330
You're mistaken!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.380
Oops, I'm sorry.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.210
That's not it at all!

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.090
Sou-nii!

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.760
Yes? What's wrong?

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:12.140
Okay, I understand. Go to Sayo-chan.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.270
Well then...

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.320
Can we talk?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.240
Oh, it's cloudy.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.120
Mm, it smells sweet.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.450
Is it an Osmanthus tree?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.750
Did you know that Osmanthus can even grow in the Himalayas?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:41.250
Although it's kind of mysterious how nostalgic it makes me feel, no matter where I smell it.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.090
I-I see...

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.920
You've been transferring from school to school this whole time, haven't you?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.840
Mihoshi-chan told me.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.430
You lived in the same apartment as her and are a year younger.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:56.390
The Ghibli-haired Saku-chan who was forever reading books and moved away while he was injured.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.810
Although I never imagined the two of you would be reunited.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.360
Mihoshi-chan's sad.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.360
T-That's not true.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.240
She has you too...

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.780
Even what happened earlier... she's probably just toying with me...

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.080
W-What is it?!

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.710
Are you in love?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.880
L-Love and stuff like that is... Er...

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.050
I meant astronomy.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.550
You should read up on it.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:33.060
The word "astronomy" or "tenmon'gaku" is made from the words "astron"

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:37.390
meaning "star" and "nemein" meaning "to name."

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.770
It's been a few thousand years since the world was created.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:45.650
However, no matter the era, the general rule for naming stars has remained unchanged.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.450
That's exactly what defines a planet.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:56.160
As time passes, you will learn more. You'll start to give names to your knowledge and emotions.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.960
I wonder what you'll call them.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.710
Mind you, this is all secondhand information garnered from Professor Akeno.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.260
Well, be nice to her.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:09.970
She's precious to me.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:13.890
Excuse me.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.390
Professor,

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.570
she sure has grown up.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.070
Yes? What's wrong?

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.650
I don't know...

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.320
I don't know, but my body moved of its own accord...

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.080
But I didn't say anything.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:40.790
What are you doing, Mihoshi?

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.250
Zipping up my mouth.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.260
Hime, there are rumors going around!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.260
Apparently, some people from a sports club saw them!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:57.060
And I was prepping for anti-mature women...

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.100
Hey, do you know where the scissors that were here went?

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.640
Can you put more care into making that?!

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.190
Done. Finished!

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:02.900
Stop yapping and work.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:06.860
I can't take it anymore! My eyes are blurry!

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.820
I bought a blueberry bread.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.650
Hang in there, Aiko.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.860
We don't have enough paint.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.400
Red paint! Red!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.030
Who stepped on this?!

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.740
What?! Is this all you've done?!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.320
This is impossible!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:18.160
We give a supporting yell to all the hard workers!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.710
What exactly is this morale-degrading racket?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:26.000
I messed up with making holes... this is my third one.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.840
The dome's nowhere near completion either!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:32.380
Allegedly, even if you mess up punching the holes, all you need to do is fill the holes using aluminum.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.470
Why couldn't you tell me this earlier?!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.090
Is this enough black curtain?

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.220
I'm sorry, but there was very little information on it.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:39.100
We might be able to get more if we ask.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:42.770
Oh, yeah. We need to cover the windows too.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.930
C-Calm down.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:43.270
It's times like this when we need to calm down.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.560
You're the one who's panicking the most.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:46.360
Can someone go and borrow the ladder?

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.360
Gotcha, President!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.190
I'll look for someone in the Cultural Festival Committee!

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.320
There's one right here!

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.700
Good afternoon.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.860
Good afternoon.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:58.240
Wow, it's absolutely chaotic everywhere...

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.450
It's due for publishing today.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.670
We've approved of the flayers you'll be handing out that day, so I'll leave them here.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.920
Okay, thank you!

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.210
I just visited the Literature Club.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.930
I see a member of the Astronomy Club is helping out.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:15.800
What?

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.340
Yes, for a bit.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.560
It looks like he was helping out quite a bit.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:27.650
That's strange. It's less than a week until the festival.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.860
The Astronomy Club should be busy making the finishing touches on their preparations too.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.530
But I'm surprised you allowed someone from the Astronomy Club to help out.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.610
I hear you all hung out together during the summer outing too.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.990
T-There is no ulterior motive.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.580
Hm... Are you ill?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.040
Your face is awfully red.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.200
Quiet!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.160
Stop yapping and get back to work!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.250
But what is there to do?

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.460
Don't wait for orders! Find work yourself!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.710
I'm sorry!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.260
Honestly...

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.760
Oh, hey.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.850
Where is everyone?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.310
We finished the manuscript, so they all headed to the printing company.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.020
How much time have you been forced to spend helping them?

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.230
I'm sorry that I didn't notice.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:15.570
I'll make sure to scold them well-

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.740
No, I'm the one who asked to help out.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.660
I really learned a lot. I had a lot of fun.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:26.660
I almost want to help out on the day itself.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:27.830
Did something happen?

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.920
There have been rumors floating around about you, Akeno and Souma-sensei.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.880
We hear about things like that in the student council too.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.680
Don't worry. I don't think I've mistaken the situation.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:46.220
I've never met him, but I do know about him.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:51.150
Someone called the police on him when he was playing with Akeno and Yarai.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.860
For a while, he was famous for that at our elementary school.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:57.650
Souma-sensei...

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:03.450
You've lived here all your life too?

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:04.280
Hm?

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.540
Well, yes. It's also a small city.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:14.750
Even though you don't talk, you still know a lot about each other.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:22.300
You live in the same city, share the same memories, and live the same times.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:29.600
It's a normal thing, but sometimes, it makes me really jealous.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:37.900
When I realized that the person I was laughing with yesterday lived a different time too,

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.910
a part of me said "Oh, I knew it," and I took a step back.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.410
I wonder why that is?

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.500
Oh, I'm sorry for chattering on.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.460
You're just really easy to talk to.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.630
Would you like to see a sample of the manuscript?

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.590
We got one copy printed.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.130
Then, do you want to join the Literature Club?

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:06.430
I'm just joking.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.470
Don't worry. You are who you are.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.530
Ooyagi-kun...

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:26.490
Makita-san?

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:31.200
U-Um... this is for you.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.250
I'm sorry if it's none of my business.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.760
I've written down everything we've done since you've been away.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.340
I'll be waiting for you.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.810
Diary of the Making of the Planaterium - Day One

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.230
Today, we designed the blueprints.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:03.110
At first, we planned to make it out of cloth, but now we're going to make it out of cardboard instead.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.780
The finished design should look something like this.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.160
Today we started making the projector.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.790
Edogawa-kun's really into this.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:17.210
We're making holes and plan to make over 500 holes.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.300
We're changing the size of the holes so the stars' brightness also changes; it's fairly hard.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:24.800
I've already ruined one...

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.090
Oh, the class is making progress too.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.430
Aiko's designs are amazing.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.180
Poo. More hole making today.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:35.440
It's tough!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.940
I think Ooyagi-kun would be good at this...

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:39.770
But I'll do my best!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:41.900
I wonder if we can all work together on the actual day.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.610
Let's all go stargazing again.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:49.120
We'll be waiting for you

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:50.450
Makita-san...

00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:00.340
Even though I can't name this feeling I'm experiencing right now...

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.420
I... can't do this anymore...

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.050
Now is now.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:04.260
I am me.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.380
Do you like all-nighters?

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.810
Let's build these small moments together!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.780
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.450
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.740
I want to tell you,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
but they just slip away…

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.920
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.500
In this Wave of Silence,

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:48.880
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.180
playing with my memories

00:22:54.180 --> 00:23:00.020
and releasing my heart.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:02.980
Into the future,

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:11.530
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.950
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:21.040
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:29.970
Listen to my “Twinkle” story!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.140
Maybe my voice would reach you.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:40.390
I look up at the sky, surrounded by Stardust!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Next time: Illuminated Ground

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:47.190
Next time on Sora no Manimani:

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:48.690
Illuminated Ground.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:49.860
So beautiful...

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.990
It's finally time for the Cultural Festival!!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.990
Did they finish the planetarium?!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:00.000
Aim to win the "Presentation Contest"

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:00.000
Let's get a telescope with the prize money!
